        },
        {
          "id": "MYS-COLONIAL",
          "text": "UNESCO distinguishes Portuguese and Dutch layers in Melaka from the British-era townscape of George Town from the late eighteenth century. This supports a bounded comparison of port heritage, rather than a complete account of colonial effects.",
